<sn><md>| **Feature**                  | **Inceptisols**                                        | **Mollisols**                                       | **Histosols**                                          |
| ---------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------ | --------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------ |
| **Meaning (Origin)**         | *Inceptum* = Beginning                                 | *Mollis* = Soft                                     | *Histos* = Tissue                                      |
| **Development Stage**        | Young, immature soils                                  | Well-developed, mature soils                        | Organic-rich soils formed under waterlogged conditions |
| **Main Horizon**             | Cambic horizon; weak ochric/mollic/umbric epipedon     | Mollic epipedon                                     | Histic epipedon                                        |
| **Dominant Parent Material** | Variable; resembles parent material                    | Base-rich parent material                           | Organic plant remains (peat)                           |
| **Dominant Vegetation**      | Variable                                               | Grasslands                                          | Wetland vegetation (mosses, grasses, etc.)             |
| **Major Pedogenic Process**  | Leaching (also illuviation, lessivage, pedoturbation)  | Melanization                                        | Ripening (physical, chemical &amp; biological)             |
| **Climate**                  | All climates except arid regions                       | Sub-humid to humid; cryic to thermic                | Cold, wet climates                                     |
| **Typical Environment**      | Glacial deposits, river valleys, floodplains, terraces | Temperate grasslands                                | Bogs, peatlands, marshes, swamps                       |
| **Organic Matter**           | Low to moderate                                        | High                                                | Very high (20–30% or more)                             |
| **Color**                    | Light to moderately colored                            | Dark-colored                                        | Dark black/brown                                       |
| **Water Holding Capacity**   | Moderate                                               | High                                                | Very high                                              |
| **Bulk Density**             | Normal                                                 | Moderate                                            | Very low (&lt;0.3 g/cm³)                                  |
| **pH**                       | Variable                                               | High (base-rich)                                    | Often acidic                                           |
| **Base Saturation (BSP)**    | Variable                                               | &gt;50%                                                | Usually low to moderate                                |
| **Clay Accumulation**        | Absent                                                 | May occur (lessivage)                               | Absent                                                 |
| **Profile Development**      | Weakly developed                                       | Well developed                                      | Very little profile development                        |
| **Soil Fertility**           | Moderate to high                                       | Very high                                           | Variable; limited by poor drainage                     |
| **Agricultural Importance**  | Productive soils                                       | Best agricultural soils                             | Productive after drainage                              |
| **Major Uses**               | Pasture, vegetables, grain crops                       | Wheat, maize, vegetables, grazing, plantation crops | Vegetables, forestry, peat, horticulture, fuel         |
| **World Distribution**       | ~9% of world's land area                               | ~6.9% of world's land area                          | ~1% of world's ice-free land area                      |
| **Bangladesh Distribution**  | Covers ~50% of Bangladesh's land area                  | Not extensive                                       | Very limited                                           |
</md></sn>